From: ROCKNIX <rocknix@rocknix.org>
Date: Mon, 20 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] spi: spi-geni-qcom: reload SPI firmware when proto mismatch in master mode

On Qualcomm SM6115-based handhelds (Mangmi Air X), the bootloader
programs GENI SE2 (4a88000.spi) with I2C microcode (proto=3) before
handing off to Linux. The SPI driver currently only calls
geni_load_se_firmware() for GENI_SE_INVALID_PROTO (0xFF), so a
chainloaded system that inherits a stale I2C/UART protocol fails
immediately with "Invalid proto 3".

Extend the master-mode firmware-reload path to cover any non-SPI
protocol value. This is safe: geni_load_se_firmware() will only proceed
if the wrapper node provides a "firmware-name" property pointing to a
valid QUP firmware blob, so boards without such a property are
unaffected.

Signed-off-by: ROCKNIX <rocknix@rocknix.org>
---
 drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c b/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
@@ -609,11 +609,8 @@ static int spi_geni_init(struct spi_geni_master *mas)
 		spi_slv_setup(mas);
-	} else if (proto == GENI_SE_INVALID_PROTO) {
+	} else if (proto != GENI_SE_SPI) {
+		/* Reload firmware for any non-SPI proto (stale I2C/UART from bootloader, or INVALID) */
 		ret = geni_load_se_firmware(se, GENI_SE_SPI);
 		if (ret) {
-			dev_err(mas->dev, "spi master firmware load failed ret: %d\n", ret);
+			dev_err(mas->dev, "spi master firmware load failed for proto %d: %d\n", proto, ret);
 			goto out_pm;
 		}
-	} else if (proto != GENI_SE_SPI) {
-		dev_err(mas->dev, "Invalid proto %d\n", proto);
-		goto out_pm;
 	}
